  "id": "landmine-reverse-lunge-knee-drive",
  "name": "Landmine Reverse Lunge to Knee Raise",
  "definition": "A source-exact reverse step lunge followed by a same-repetition free-leg knee drive while the front foot stays planted. Both hands cup the anchored landmine sleeve at upper-chest height; the rear foot steps back, the athlete rises on the planted leg and lifts that free knee near hip height, then controls the raised leg for the next repetition; the exact inter-repetition reset is unreported. The anchored bar follows its lever arc and only added plates are logged on the same setup. A plain reverse lunge returning to two feet, front-rack or elbow-crease holds, and unanchored barbell lunges remain outside this family.",
